In article <Czt8zv.4vv@un.seqeb.gov.au>, al012@svtstu.seqeb.gov.au (Anthony) writes:
|>Dear all,
|>
|>I am trying to port an ULTRIX program to OSF.  The program basically
|>uses a packetfilter to send and receives packets from a PDP11.  
|>I am getting unaligned error messages and it is not receiving packets
|>from the PDP11.  I used kill -9 on the process but it refuses to
|>terminate.  Has anyone else come across this problem before ?
-- 
Use the following option with the packetfilter, and you won't hang

      ioctl(fd,BIOCSRTIMEOUT,&timeout);

If a read times out, it will return a status of 0, so you just queue
another.  Finding the unaligned errors will be easier if the process doesn't
hang;-)
