I just put one on a 700 running 3.0.  Seems to work fine.  We are swapping there
plus a couple of partitions.  I'm not much of an osf expert, but here are a
couple of things that seem a bit strange but seem to be ok:
-->>>sho dev   will show you this device as being a 500Mb drive.  Apparently
sho dev can't figure out what this drive is.  The same thing happens with the 
seagate 9gb drive.  I don't think this matters one way or another.
--Once you have run MAKEDEV and copied the label from the driver, if you look
at the label you will see (at least the way I did it) that the rpm value
in the label is 3600.  Well the drive is spec'd at something like 5400.  
Of course you can edit the label and set rpm to whatever you feel like, but
what actual difference it makes I don't know.  I have a call into dec, but so
far have no answer.
So in sum, I just followed the bonehead approach of letting osf figure things
out for itself and everything seems to be fine.  If anyone has any comments on
the above, I'd love to hear them.


