A simple lock aquired by a loadable subsystem component may panic due to a
sign extension problem.  That is, the sign bit replication of a 32 bit value
in a 64 bit field causes lock information to be corrupted that may panic a
kernel in lockmodes 0, 1, 2, and 3 under heavy load.  At lockmode 4 the kernel
will always panic.

A system exhibiting this fault (non lockmode 4) will have a message
similar to the following:

