The latest version of xv is v 3.0c. 3.01 is a hack created by someone
else (Both 3.0b and 3.0c is actually released *after* 3.01). If I
remember it right 3.01 is really 3.0a patched so that it can read XPM
files.

Anyway, I've compiled several versions of xv 3.x under OSF/1 2.x, and
it has worked every time (except the tiff-library). The tiff-library
that is delivered with all versions of xv (this *may* change when xv
3.10 is released) is incompatible with 64-bit longs. I've tested to
compile it under OSF/1 3.0, and had no problem at all.

I have a version that reads tiff-files, but I had to replace the
tiff-library with a newer (beta) version, and do some small changes in
xvtiff.c. The binary for OSF/1 3.0 is approximately 1.1 MB.


