I think the best approach is to put all local startup stuff in rc3.d. Give 
them names starting with S## and usually a number in the range 90-99. Just be 
sure you put it after things you need- like the network, or other daemons.

I would not put things like httpd in inittab. 

For things you want to shutdown properly, place K## scripts in rc0.d.

CAUTION: using 'shutdown -r now' or 'shutdown -h now' does NOT execute the 
rc0.d directory as you would guess. It simply shuts down the system processes. 
Doing 'shutdown now' DOES run thru rc0.d, but then it stops at single user 
mode, so if you want to do a reboot you must then go to the console terminal.

This is a pain, but it is explicit, if well hidden, in the shutdown man page.

ron ginger


