In article <3avsqo$131s@unix1.sncc.lsu.edu>, pradeep@phzeus.phys.lsu.edu (Pradeep Balachandran) writes:
> 
> Hi 
> 
> I need to add swap space for an Alpha running OSF/1.  Do I have to do a 
> newfs on the swap partition 

no

> or is it enough if I just alter the partition
> table using disklabel.  

might work, if you know *exactly* what you're doing :-) (read: reduced the 
right other partition before)

I'd rather suggest to add another partition as second swap space:

- be sure that the chosen partition is empty/backed up and unmounted

- edit /etc/fstab as follows:
  /dev/rz3b       swap1   ufs sw 0 2   # default swap partition
  /dev/rz3g       swap2   ufs sw 0 2   # rz3g as *example* for 2nd swap space

- enter 'swapon -a' (that's it, no reboot)

regards,
Eric


