>I am getting unaligned error messages and it is not receiving packets
>from the PDP11.  I used kill -9 on the process but it refuses to
>terminate.  Has anyone else come across this problem before ?
>

	Any process waiting in the kernel won't see the kill -9 until
	it "comes out".

	If the unaligned errors are always reporting the same
	addresses, I'd fire up a new copy of the program, examine
	where the unaligned accesses are coming from using YFD (Your
	Favorite Debugger).  If there's a correlation between the two
	problems, you may discover that the data-structure you're
	passing into the kernel is malformed.  Fix that and "Bob's
	your Uncle".  [Or is that only an English idiom and not found
	elsewhere in the Commonwealth?]

