In article <Maurice.Steyvers.181.785080315@ica.rulimburg.nl>, Maurice.Steyvers@ica.rulimburg.nl (Maurice Steyvers) writes:
> 
> Is it possible to have our users work (with only one username to login) 
> under different projects (and thus different directories, but not different
> filesystems) and to have quotas for as well the users home-directories and
> the several project directories.
> So user john works under project1 and project2 plus in his private home-
> directorie. The files john creates when working at project1 must fall
> under quota for project1, the files he creates when working at project2
> must fall under quota for project2 and so on... 
> What i don't want is more usernames for just one user.
> 
> How can i establish this...?
> 
> Any help/tips appreciated...
> 

You can put the user into multiple groups.  A user can change his primary group
with the newgrp command.  Files are created with the new primary group.  Quotas
operate on groups as well as users.

The group id is also logged in pacct process accounting files, but may not be 
readily accessible with the supplied procedures.  You can always write your own.

Sam Bair
Ohio Supercomputer Center


