Hello

I didn't receive any replies to my postings about problems with dms clients,
eg LAT not being configured, with OSF/1 V3.0,. but I thought I'd post the
solution anyway.

I must admit I was starting to think dms was a bit of a sick joke :-(

Anyway, just now I discovered that to do a partial or full kernel build
for a dataless dms client one must use doconfig -n, which builds both
vmunix and .vmunix (the network kernel) on a client system running the generic
kernel for that dms environment. Then move these into / on the client system.

I was running with generic .vmunix and customized vmunix which was just about
working but had several problems.

I discovered this option with man doconfig. It is not documented anywhere
I can find in the hardcopy OSF/1 V3.0 docs.

Hope this might help someone.

btw dms is not quite clustering as OpenVMS people know it, but an improvement
on upgrading each and every OSF/1 box separately.



