In article <3a08qq$35q@pipe1.pipeline.com>, kenjo@nytimes.com (Ken Johnston) writes:

>Does anyone know if you can mirror the root partition disk under OSF1?

I had expected the LSM SPD to say one way or the other, but it
doesn't.  IF mirroring the root partition with LSM is supported
then you'll need at least V3.0.  The other documentation I have
is all for V2.0 where shadowing of the root wasn't supported.

> Second: Is OSF1 bootable from an external drive on DEC hardware?

OSF/1 is bootable from any supported disk with the exception of
the RZ24L, RZ55 and RA60 (taken from the V3.0 SPD).  Whether
internal or external doesn't matter.  It will probably boot
from most well-behaved 3rd party SCSI disks.

> Third: With disk mirroring, is there completely automatic failover to the
>secondary disk?

The shadowing available with LSM supports 2-8 members in the array.  For
reading, I'm pretty sure that I/Os are distributed among all the members
of the array.  So the loss of a member just means that it won't get any
I/Os.  There's no "failover" involved.

