The following method was described by marant@univ-lille1.fr (Dominique
Marant) and seems to work.

 - set the flag '8' in the mailers description:
      For example:  Msmtpr, P=[IPC], F=mDFMuX8, S=13, R=23, A=IPC $h, E=\r\n

>Is sendmail so lame as to only deal with 7bit data (pretty sad
>given the system is fairly new and 8bit isn't rocket science) or is it
>just due to a bad config ?

sendmail 8.6.9 handles this without problems (unless you tell it to
strip the 8 bit). We uses sendmail 8.6.9 on our mailhub since DEC's
sendmail can't handle DNS'es that do negative cacheing (at least the
version delivered with DEC OSF/1 2.x can't).

The problem isn't really sendmail, it's the resolver that misbehaves
but I couldn't fix that without relinking (actually it might have been
possible using methods that I didn't know of then).

On all other machines we run a simplistic sendmail.cf that sends all
mail to the mailhub, so they still uses DEC's sendmail (if I hadn't
already fixed the 8bit problem I would have replaced them too).


