asedit-1.3.2 patch is available

A patch for asedit-1.31 is available in the following places:

	ftp.x.org (198.112.44.100) in /contrib/editors/asedit-1.31_1.3.2.patch.Z
	or in Europe:
	src.doc.ic.ac.uk (146.169.2.10) in   /packages/X11-contrib/editors/asedit-1.31_1.3.2.patch.Z

and from several other ftp sites.

This patch brings asedit 1.31 to asedit 1.3.2.

You can also get the full 1.3.2 Release as "asedit-1.3.2.tar.Z" 
from the same places.


What
----
Asedit is an easy to use text editor for X Window System and Motif.
Version 1.3.2, International Free Release, includes the following language
versions: English, Danish, Dutch, French, German, Polish, Portuguese
and Swedish. All commands and messages are localized for each
language. The on-line help is available only in English.


Release Date
------------
10 November 1994


What is added/fixed
-------------------
Here's a short list of added features and bug fixes:

    Command line option "-v" opens now the file(s) in view-only mode.
 
    File|New and File|Open commands modified slightly: a new window
    is now NOT created when text has not been entered yet and most users
    expect the current window to be used (see HISTORY for details).

    Addition of three new values for the extend selection parameter: 
    EXTEND_TO_WHOLE_FILE, USE_WHOLE_FILE and USE_FILE_OR_SELECTION. 
    All of them might be used in filter extension definition.
    The spell command was redefined using USE_FILE_OR_SELECTION value.

    Sensitivity of the paste button in the pop-up menu in the spawned
    windows corrected.

    The default print range option and default options inside replace
    and find dialogs are now set via resources (so user can customize them).
    The default printing command is also set in the resource file.

    intervalId in exec_cmd.c now declared as XtIntervalId instead of int
    (caused dump on OSF/1 V2.0 when filters where used).



