Sorry, I forgot to say how to setup the printcap file:

With lprsetup you have to select the printer type 'remote'. It's the
same to print with an ethernet printer and to print via a remote workstation.
The remote name ('rm') is the printer name, which you have to add to the
/etc/hosts database and the remote printer ('lp') is 'text' for text
printing and 'raw' for postscript and HPGL. Your printcap entry should
be like:

4|lp4|hplaser|HPLASER:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp4err:\
        :lp=:\
        :rm=hplaser:\
        :rp=raw:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd4:
5|lp5|hplaser_text:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp5err:\
        :lp=:\
        :rm=hplaser:\
        :rp=text:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd5:

with printer 4 for PS and 5 for text.

Hope this will help you,

Volker


