>dated 1/13/94.  My program has a realloc error on this system (tries to
>realloc 64 bytes).  However, on a newer (V3.0) system, there is no problem
>at all: cc -V shows malloc.c version 4.2.11.7 from 4/5/1994.  It seems that
>malloc.c has gone through quite a few changes in a 3 month period.  Was a
>bug fixed that my program is seeing in version 4.2.9.12?

Highly unlikely. More likely is that there is a bug in your program that
is sensitive to details of the malloc implementation (common errors like
writing past the end of allocated space are an example of this - depending
on what you tromp on, the mistake can be either benign or fatal.)

Install the ATOM program analysis tools that are distributed on the
operating system CD; the Third Degree tool is an excellent aid in finding
the cause of memory allocation errors.

>   If this cannot be answered, who do I talk to?
Well, if you can reproduce your error with a simple case, you could talk
to the support center.
