NEdit is a popular GUI-style programming and plain-text editor for X/Motif
systems.  It has a very complete command set based on successful Macintosh and
MS Windows text editors, yet remains one of the easiest to learn Unix or VMS
editors available.  NEdit is free in both source and executable form, via
anonymous ftp to ftp.fnal.gov in the /pub/nedit directory.  Pre-built, tested,
executables are available for SGI, DEC (OSF/1, Ultrix, VMS, Alpha-VMS), IBM
AIX, Sun (Solaris and SunOS), and HP systems.

Version 3.1.1 is a maintenence release which fixes a couple of minor glitches
in the 3.1 release of October 1st.

Benefits over 3.1:

1) Fixes keysyms for the Delete and Insert keys (NEdit prints a warning, and
   the Cut and/or Copy and Paste accelerators don't work) on some systems
  
2) Fixes Open... dialog not remembering where the last file was opened from,
   on systems with newer Motif 1.2 libraries
  
3) Protects users from a potentially dangerous bug in unpatched versions of
   AIX 3.2.5
   
If you have none of the above problems, you don't need to fetch this release,
however, all AIX users are advised to upgrade as a precaution against possible
data loss.

