I've recently configured a DFS environment using DEC DCE 1.3 on OSF/1
3.0.  We are using HP-UX 9.05 and AIX 3.2.5 DFS clients and an AXP
3000/500 as a server.  

We are using AdvFS volumes for the DFS server backing storage. This
allows us to mount the filesets locally. The AdvFS filesystem
is supporting mounts from three different network file protocols:

	Native DFS, NFS and Columbia Appletalk (AUFS)


Has anyone else tried exporting the same volume BOTH over DFS and
NFS at the same time ???   We are currently prototyping this
environment for our group and hope that it will lead to a long-term
filesystem solution for our whole company. If you've had similar
experiences, please post followups to this describing what you've
learned and what problems you've encountered.


Also, we found that AMD provides an excellent solution to maintain
a uniform namespace of sparse NFS resources. We designed our file
namespace to support a mixture of DFS and NFS components with
administrative ease. It seems that engineering the filesystem
namespace and standardizing on it makes sense as the first step
in using a networked filesystem technology.

